# Patch-ID: P-TAB-001 (slice S2) — browser-less TabRegistry + TabSession + delegate skeleton
# Area: tab (area dir introduced by tab/006; see its header).
# Rationale: The centerpiece decision of P-TAB-001-SLICES §2: a browser-less
#   registry, NOT a BrowserWindowInterface adapter. TabFeatures::Init CHECKs a
#   BrowserWindowInterface (tab_features.cc:276) and reaching it requires
#   TabStripModel → tabs::TabModel, i.e. ~69 virtuals of browser-window
#   semantics ReArc does not have — the fake-window route is forbidden (R6).
#   The registry route never reaches the CHECK: TabSession owns a
#   content::WebContents created directly via WebContents::Create.
# Additive only: no upstream hunks. Files:
#   - tab_registry.{h,cc} — singleton registry: engine-side monotonic uint64
#     tab_id allocation (IPC-CONTRACT §3: "E allocates tab_id"), session map,
#     FIFO command envelope + in-order application (producers arrive with
#     S3's IPC layer; day-one nothing posts), idempotent DestroySession with
#     DEFERRED destruction (posted, so delegate/observer callbacks unwind
#     first — P-TAB-001's destruction-from-callback prohibition), and
#     DestroyAllSessions as the teardown-ordering primitive (sessions die
#     before profile release; the call site lands in a later slice because
#     P-APP-001's finalization file is frozen).
#   - tab_session.{h,cc} — one unique_ptr<content::WebContents> + one
#     ReArcTabDelegate (created first, set immediately after Create), space/
#     order metadata, guarded close-state machine (kOpen → kCloseRequested →
#     kUnloadPending → kClosed, veto paths back to kOpen; S6 owns the real
#     pipeline), monotonic content-generation counter. Start hidden: a fresh
#     WebContents is hidden by default and only the S4 lease makes it
#     visible. Never exposes WebContents* across the bridge boundary
#     (web_contents() is bridge-internal; shell identity is tab_id only).
#   - tab_delegate.{h,cc} — ReArcTabDelegate : content::WebContentsDelegate,
#     ONE PER SESSION (never a singleton: delegate callbacks carry no tab
#     identity beyond the WebContents*). Day-one override set is exactly the
#     set P-TAB-001 lists, each with an audited safe default (R7: cancel
#     through upstream callbacks, never hang):
#       OpenURLFromTab — CURRENT_TAB routed for real (content-shell pattern,
#         shell.cc:473-478: LoadURLWithParams + navigation-handle callback +
#         return source); NEW_*/SINGLETON rejected (nullptr + VLOG; S6 owns
#         adoption); OFF_THE_RECORD/SAVE_TO_DISK/IGNORE_ACTION rejected.
#       AddNewContents — predictable rejection: nullptr, *was_blocked=true,
#         moved-in WebContents destroyed on scope exit (S6 owns adoption).
#       ActivateContents — no-op + VLOG (no focus stealing).
#       IsContentsActive — true (content's documented browser-less semantic,
#         restated explicitly).
#       CloseContents — no-op + VLOG (shell owns tab lifetime; "Window.close
#         only detaches/hides tabs" — detachment is S6).
#       BeforeUnloadFired — *proceed_to_fire_unload = false (conservative
#         cancel; content's default allows).
#       NavigationStateChanged / LoadingStateChanged — deliberately quiet
#         (S3's observer surface owns events).
#       TakeFocus — false (content default; lease routing arrives with S4).
#       GetJavaScriptDialogManager — nullptr (audited at pin:
#         RunBeforeUnloadConfirm resolves (false, true) with no manager;
#         CancelDialogs null-safe — callbacks complete, beforeunload vetoed).
#         S5's rearc_javascript_dialog_manager is the real manager; per
#         P-TAB-001, "returning null alone is not proof of that policy".
# R6 helper policy (recorded here per the slice plan's "each recorded in the
#   patch header" rule): NO TabHelpers::AttachTabHelpers (legacy), NO
#   TabFeatures, NO PreventFeatureInitializationForTesting bypass. The
#   whitelisted per-helper CreateForWebContents set is EMPTY day-one: the
#   first candidate (CoreTabHelper) lives in //chrome/browser/ui/tab_contents/
#   and :core cannot dep on //chrome/browser/ui (layering runs ui → core), so
#   the whitelist decision moves to the S5 service-adapter audits.
# Profile keepalive: TabSession stores the BrowserContext borrowed (caller
#   guarantees it outlives the session; DestroyAllSessions runs before
#   profile release). ScopedProfileKeepAlive
#   (chrome/browser/profiles/keep_alive/scoped_profile_keep_alive.h) wiring
#   lands with the embedded-startup integration wave; S2 records the
#   dependency instead of faking a keepalive it cannot correctly own yet.
#   Recorded in the P-TAB-001-SLICES drift log.
# S4 attachment lease: deliberately NOT a TabSession member — tab/007's files
#   freeze at landing (series-mechanics invariant), so S4 associates leases
#   through its own tab_id-keyed map, same additive pattern as tab/006's
#   native-window provider seam.
# Hunk placement (series mechanics): the only upstream-file hunk is a sources
#   block in chrome/browser/BUILD.gn's is_mac list between
#   "browser_process_platform_part_mac.mm" and
#   "chrome_browser_application_mac.mm" — disjoint -U3 windows from tab/006's
#   block (icon_loader→memory_details) and app/005's block. Sources join
#   :core (rearc_bridge/BUILD.gn is app/002's frozen file); no new deps
#   (:core already has //base and content).
# Compile-level only: scaffolding skeleton; runtime tab creation additionally
#   needs the P-APP-001 embedded-startup profile seam (a loaded
#   Profile*/BrowserContext to pass in) — per slice-plan §5, no live-tab
#   validation this wave.
# Last rebased: Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca8a) + overlay 001-006.
# Gate evidence: engine/build-p7.log exit 0 (attempt 2; attempt 1 added the
#   base::NoDestructor friend declaration).
